{
 "format": 1,
 "version": "1.9.0",
 "min_shell": 1,
 "notes": [
  "Sent something to your PC or Chromebook? It's copied for you, ready to paste, and a little card shows what came. On a Chromebook you can also have files saved into a folder in Files (Settings > What arrives here).",
  "Copying from your PC to the Chromebook works even when Vault wasn't the window you clicked last: it copies as soon as you click in Vault, or gives you a Copy button.",
  "Bold, Italic, Underline, Strikethrough and Highlight buttons in notes (Ctrl+B, Ctrl+I, Ctrl+U), and Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y undo and redo every change.",
  "On your PC, the note-taker can write down what's playing on the PC \u2014 a video, an online class or a call. Pick \"PC sound\" (needs Jarvis 1.1.2).",
  "Gemini answers in seconds, and the Claude tab is now called Chat."
 ],
